class:: VectorPhaseOsc
summary:: Piecewise vector phaseshaping oscillator
categories:: UGens>Generators>Deterministic
related:: Guides/NovelOscillators

description::

VectorPhaseOsc maps a signed linear phase through as many as eight movable
two-dimensional breakpoints before reading a sine. It is an original
implementation of the vector-phaseshaping technique described by Kleimola,
Lazzarini, Timoney, and Välimäki. Breakpoint pairs are sorted by their x
positions and sanitized every sample into a strictly increasing input
sequence; each y value stays attached to its corresponding x value.
Oversampling plus a maximum-segment-slope fade reduce the most severe aliases.

The closest vanilla UGen is link::Classes/SinOsc::. Neutral breakpoints reproduce
a sine, while non-neutral points redistribute phase speed within every cycle.

classmethods::

method:: ar

argument:: freq
Signed frequency in hertz.

argument:: x
One to eight input-phase breakpoint positions. Values are sorted, clamped away
from the endpoints, and made strictly increasing.

argument:: y
An array matching code::x:: in length. Values are clamped to code::0..1::.

argument:: phaseMod
Readout phase modulation in radians, applied before the segment map without
changing accumulated phase.

argument:: sync
A nonpositive-to-positive edge resets accumulated phase before producing that
sample.

argument:: oversample
Initialization-rate factor code::1::, code::2::, or code::4::.

argument:: mul
Output multiplier.

argument:: add
Offset added after multiplication.

returns::
One audio signal.

method:: kr

VectorPhaseOsc is audio-rate only. This method throws an error.

subsection:: Discussion

Implicit endpoints code::[0, 0]:: and code::[1, 1]:: preserve cycle
continuity. Very short segments imply very high instantaneous frequency; the
oscillator fades a mapping as its maximum segment frequency reaches Nyquist.

examples::

code::
(
{ VectorPhaseOsc.ar(110, [0.5], [0.5]) * 0.08 }.play;
)
::

code::
(
{
    VectorPhaseOsc.ar(
        70,
        [0.18, 0.62, 0.86],
        [
            LFNoise1.kr(0.2).range(0.08, 0.35),
            0.72,
            LFNoise1.kr(0.13).range(0.75, 0.98)
        ],
        oversample: 4
    ) * 0.07;
}.play;
)
::

